# Reva Full System — Implementation Plan

This document details every change required to bring the existing Reva codebase (FastAPI + Celery + Redis + Supabase + Claude/Ollama) to the complete 10-layer architecture described in the specification.

---

## Current State (What Already Exists)

| Layer | Status | What's Built |
|---|---|---|
| Lead Ingestion | 🟡 Partial | WhatsApp (360dialog, Evolution), Telegram webhook parsers. No unified gateway, no signature verification |
| Task Queue | 🟢 Done | Celery + Redis broker. Basic retry (3 retries, flat 5s). Idempotency via Redis |
| AI Core | 🟢 Done | Claude Sonnet + Ollama with tool calling (search_inventory, book_meeting, send_properties). System prompt as "Amara Okonkwo" |
| Intelligence | 🟡 Partial | Lagos-aware inventory search with ±20% budget flexibility. LLM-based seriousness scoring. No behavioural scoring, no anti-hallucination monitor |
| Data Layer | 🟢 Done | Supabase (leads, properties, units, agents, tenants, developments) + Redis cache (history, stage, lead data, matches). RLS enabled but no policies |
| Routing & Handoff | 🟡 Partial | Round-robin agent assignment. Score-based routing stub. CLOSED/PAUSE/RESUME commands. No TAKEOVER/HANDBACK/STATUS |
| Background Jobs | 🟡 Partial | Nurture job (daily 10am, 3/7/14-day). No resurrection, portal sync, or ROI report jobs |
| Observability | 🟡 Partial | Health endpoint (Redis + Supabase + LLM breaker). Circuit breakers (LLM, DB). No Prometheus, Grafana, or WhatsApp breaker |
| Client Surfaces | 🟡 Partial | Static HTML/CSS/JS dashboard with kanban + stats. No Next.js, no admin panel |
| Infrastructure | 🟡 Partial | 4 SQL migrations, Celery config, APScheduler. No RLS policies, no structured logging |

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Build Sequence Prioritisation**: This plan follows the spec's build sequence (Weeks 3–4 → Month 2 → Month 3). Phases 1–5 are Week 3–4 scope. If you want to reorder or defer any phase, please flag it now.

> [!WARNING]
> **Breaking Change — Agent Commands**: The current [agent_commands.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/agent_commands.py) uses the lead's phone number. The spec calls for a separate agent control WhatsApp number. This requires distinguishing agent messages from lead messages at the webhook level, which means either a second WhatsApp number or a middleware check against the [agents](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/agent_notify.py#50-52) table.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Dashboard Rebuild**: The spec calls for a Next.js + Tailwind live dashboard on Vercel. This is a ~full frontend project. The current static HTML dashboard works and could remain as the MVP while the Next.js version is built as a separate repo. Do you want the Next.js dashboard as part of this plan or as a separate effort?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gmail API**: Portal email intercept and ROI reports both require Google Cloud project setup + OAuth credentials. These are infrastructure pre-requisites you'll need to provision. Same for Vapi.ai and Meta Graph API keys.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 1 — Core Infrastructure Hardening

This phase makes the ingestion pipeline robust by adding the unified gateway, signature verification, proper retry policies, and moving rate-limiting/dedup to the gateway level.

---

#### [NEW] [gateway.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/gateway.py)

The unified ingestion gateway. Single entry point for all channels. Does five things before any message touches the AI:

1. **Normalise**: Convert any source-specific payload into [IncomingMessage](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/models/lead.py#21-28)
2. **Deduplicate**: Check `msg:{message_id}` key in Redis (1-hour TTL)
3. **Rate limit**: 10 messages per 60 seconds per phone number (already in [redis.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/cache/redis.py), wired in here)
4. **Verify signature**: HMAC validation per provider (360dialog, Evolution, Telegram)
5. **Dispatch**: Drop to Celery queue, return 200

This replaces the duplicated dispatch logic currently in [whatsapp.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/whatsapp.py) (lines 146–195) and [telegram.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/telegram.py).

---

#### [MODIFY] [whatsapp.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/whatsapp.py)

- Remove Celery dispatch logic from [whatsapp_360dialog_webhook](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/whatsapp.py#146-170) and [whatsapp_evolution_webhook](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/whatsapp.py#172-196)
- Both routes call `gateway.ingest()` instead
- Add webhook signature verification middleware (HMAC-SHA256 for 360dialog, custom header for Evolution)

#### [MODIFY] [telegram.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/webhooks/telegram.py)

- Remove Celery dispatch logic
- Call `gateway.ingest()` with `source="telegram"`
- Add Telegram bot token signature verification (`X-Telegram-Bot-Api-Secret-Token` header)

#### [MODIFY] [celery_app.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/workers/celery_app.py)

- Add exponential backoff retry policy: `task_default_retry_delay=5`, `task_max_retries=3`
- Configure dead-letter queue: failed tasks route to `dead_letter` queue
- Add `task_reject_on_worker_lost=True` for reliability

#### [MODIFY] [tasks.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/workers/tasks.py)

- Update [process_message_task](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/workers/tasks.py#135-145) decorator: `autoretry_for=(Exception,)`, `retry_backoff=5`, `retry_backoff_max=125`
- Add dead-letter callback: on max retries exceeded, dispatch alert (WhatsApp to on-call number)
- Remove inline idempotency check (moved to gateway)

#### [MODIFY] [redis.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/cache/redis.py)

- Add `mark_message_processed(message_id)` with 1-hour TTL (gateway dedup)
- Add `is_message_processed(message_id)` check

