### Phase 2 — AI Core & Intelligence Services

Adds the anti-hallucination monitor, Whisper voice transcription, behavioural scoring, and the intent extraction service.

---

#### [NEW] [anti_hallucination.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/llm/anti_hallucination.py)

Post-generation checker. Scans Reva's response for:
- Property names → cross-reference against [properties](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/inventory.py#220-333) and [units](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/routers/inventory.py#14-21) tables
- Prices (₦ or number patterns) → verify against inventory
- Locations → verify only mentioned locations that exist in inventory

If hallucination detected, block the response and replace with fallback message pushing toward booking.

#### [NEW] [transcription.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/transcription.py)

Whisper API integration for voice note transcription:
- Accept audio URL, download media, send to OpenAI Whisper
- Support English, Nigerian Pidgin, Yoruba, Igbo (via `language` hint)
- Return transcript text that feeds into the conversation as if typed
- Replace the placeholder `transcribe_voice_note` import in [tasks.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/workers/tasks.py)

#### [NEW] [scoring.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/scoring.py)

Behavioural lead scoring engine. Two signal types:
- **Conversation score**: Already extracted by LLM as `seriousness_score` (1–10)
- **Behavioural score**: Calculated from response speed (time between messages), message volume, keyword signals ("payment plan", "C of O", "school nearby", "when can I visit")

Combined score = weighted average. Score determines routing (8+ → senior agent, 5–7 → standard, <5 → nurture).

#### [MODIFY] [extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/services/extractor.py)

Currently a stub (`# Intent extraction logic\n`). Implement:
- Intent classification (buying, renting, investing, just browsing)
- Urgency detection (timeline keywords)
- Budget extraction from natural language
- Complement the LLM's `<<<EXTRACTED>>>` block with rule-based fallback

#### [MODIFY] [client.py](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/llm/client.py)

- Wire `llm_breaker.call()` around [call_claude()](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/llm/client.py#58-101) and [call_ollama()](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/llm/client.py#40-56) in [get_ai_response](file:///c:/Users/ZBOOK%20STUDIO%20G5/Documents/dev/reva/app/llm/client.py#202-302)
- Add anti-hallucination check after response generation, before returning
- Add structured timing (duration logged on every LLM call)

